<resources>
    <!--
         ★ An EMPTY default home screen: no icons, no widgets, no folders, no
         hotseat, no search bar, no clock. Owner's decision (OPEN-ISSUES.md #32a,
         confirmed session 24 as "上面什么东西都不要有").

         ── ⚠️ WHY THIS IS AN RRO AND NOT AutoInstallsLayout ─────────────────

         MalbecParts used to do this through AutoInstallsLayout — a
         PLAY_AUTO_INSTALL marker receiver plus a res/xml layout. That mechanism
         CANNOT express "empty", and the tree asserted for three sessions that it
         could. Measured on the flashed build in session 24: with an empty
         <workspace/> the home screen came up with Launcher3's own default
         (Contacts/Calendar/Gallery/Music/Camera hotseat, the Google search
         widget, the clock, a Google folder and Play Store).

         The reason is one branch, ModelDbController.java:557-563:

             if ((mOpenHelper.loadFavorites(db, loader) <= 0)
                     && usingExternallyProvidedLayout) {
                 // Unable to load external layout. Cleanup and load the internal layout.
                 mOpenHelper.createEmptyDB(db);
                 mOpenHelper.loadFavorites(db, getDefaultLayoutParser(widgetHolder));
             }

         An external layout that inserts ZERO items is indistinguishable from one
         that failed to parse, so Launcher3 throws it away and loads its own.
         "Empty" is the one thing that route cannot say.

         ── What this does instead ───────────────────────────────────────────

         It replaces the INTERNAL default. InvariantDeviceProfile hands
         DefaultLayoutParser `mIdp.defaultLayoutId` (ModelDbController.java:581-584),
         which device_profiles.xml points at one of the resources below. Pointing
         every one of them at an empty <favorites/> means loadFavorites() returns 0
         on a path where `usingExternallyProvidedLayout` is false, so the branch
         above never runs and zero items is the accepted answer.

         ⚠️ ALL of them, not just the current grid. `idp_grid_name` reads
         `6_by_5` on this unit today, but the grid is user-selectable in the
         launcher's own settings, and overriding only the current one would mean
         the icons silently come back the day someone changes it. Launcher3's
         res/xml/ has exactly these eleven; if a future release adds one, add it
         here too.

         ⚠️ The AutoInstallsLayout half was REMOVED rather than left alongside
         this: MalbecParts no longer claims PLAY_AUTO_INSTALL and no longer ships
         a default_layout resource. Two mechanisms racing to define the same
         thing is how the "empty means empty" claim survived three sessions
         without being true.
    -->
    <item type="xml" name="default_workspace_2x2">@xml/empty_workspace</item>
    <item type="xml" name="default_workspace_3x3">@xml/empty_workspace</item>
    <item type="xml" name="default_workspace_4x5">@xml/empty_workspace</item>
    <item type="xml" name="default_workspace_5x5">@xml/empty_workspace</item>
    <item type="xml" name="default_workspace_5x6">@xml/empty_workspace</item>
    <item type="xml" name="default_workspace_5x7">@xml/empty_workspace</item>
    <item type="xml" name="default_workspace_5x8">@xml/empty_workspace</item>
    <item type="xml" name="default_workspace_6x5">@xml/empty_workspace</item>
    <item type="xml" name="default_workspace_6x6">@xml/empty_workspace</item>
    <item type="xml" name="default_workspace_7x3">@xml/empty_workspace</item>
    <item type="xml" name="default_workspace_8x3">@xml/empty_workspace</item>
</resources>
